<%#
  Rendered with layout: false — the application layout's header calls out to
  tuber for queue depth and ingest health, which is pointless work for a page
  that exists to say "a variable is missing". Styles are inline for the same
  reason: this page has to render even if something upstream of the asset
  pipeline is unhappy.
%><!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>Splat — authentication misconfigured</title>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        min-height: 100vh;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        padding: 2rem 1rem;
        background: #f9fafb;
        color: #111827;
        font-family: ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }
      .card {
        max-width: 34rem;
        width: 100%;
        background: #fff;
        border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
        border-radius: 0.5rem;
        padding: 1.5rem;
      }
      h1 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
      p { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-size: 0.925rem; }
      ul { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
      li { font-size: 0.925rem; }
      code {
        font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace;
        font-size: 0.85em;
        background: #f3f4f6;
        border-radius: 0.25rem;
        padding: 0.1rem 0.3rem;
      }
      .muted { color: #6b7280; font-size: 0.825rem; }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        body { background: #030712; color: #f3f4f6; }
        .card { background: #111827; border-color: #1f2937; }
        code { background: #1f2937; }
        .muted { color: #9ca3af; }
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="card">
      <h1>🐛💥 Authentication is half-configured</h1>

      <p>
        Splat found some OpenID Connect settings but not all of them, so it can't tell
        whether this instance is meant to be open or protected. Rather than guess and
        serve the UI unauthenticated, it is refusing to serve it at all.
      </p>

      <p>Set the missing variables and restart:</p>
      <ul>
        <% SplatAuthorization.missing_oidc_vars.each do |var| %>
          <li><code><%= var %></code></li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>

      <p>
        To run Splat deliberately open instead, unset <em>all</em> of
        <code><%= SplatAuthorization::OIDC_VARS.join("</code>, <code>").html_safe %></code>.
      </p>

      <p class="muted">
        Event ingestion, <code>/_health</code> and <code>/mcp</code> are unaffected and
        still accepting data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
